<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Object Detection and Instance Segmentation on COCO</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Setup.</span>
We adopt Mask R-CNN <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib66" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite> with FPN, training on COCO <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">train2017</span> and reporting on <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">val2017</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib65" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite>. We use the standard <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1{\times}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1{\times}</annotation></semantics></math> (12-epoch, single-scale) and <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="3{\times}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3{\times}</annotation></semantics></math>+MS (36-epoch, multi-scale) schedules with AdamW at initial learning rate <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1{\times}10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1{\times}10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math> and batch size 16. Backbones are initialized from ImageNet-1K pretraining; the rest of the detector is randomly initialized. All experiments are implemented in MMDetection <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib76" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>]</cite>. FLOPs are reported at <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1280{\times}800" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1280</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>800</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1280{\times}800</annotation></semantics></math> input, and we report box AP (<math id="S4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{AP^{b}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>AP</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{AP^{b}}</annotation></semantics></math>), <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{AP^{b}_{50}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>AP</mi><mn>50</mn><mi>b</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{AP^{b}_{50}}</annotation></semantics></math>, mask AP (<math id="S4.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{AP^{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>AP</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{AP^{m}}</annotation></semantics></math>), and <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{AP^{m}_{50}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>AP</mi><mn>50</mn><mi>m</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{AP^{m}_{50}}</annotation></semantics></math> for both schedules.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Results.</span>
Table <a href="#S4.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 4.3 Semantic Segmentation on ADE20K ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Can Graphs Help Vision SSMs See Better?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> summarizes COCO performance. Under the <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1{\times}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1{\times}</annotation></semantics></math> schedule, GraphScan-Mamba-T/S/B achieve box mAP of <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="49.1/50.7/51.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>49.1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>50.7</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>51.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">49.1/50.7/51.9</annotation></semantics></math>, outperforming VMamba-T/S/B by <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.8/2.0/2.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.8</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2.0</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2.7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.8/2.0/2.7</annotation></semantics></math>, Swin-T/S/B by <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6.4/5.9/5.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>6.4</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>5.9</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>5.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6.4/5.9/5.0</annotation></semantics></math>, and ConvNeXt-T/S/B by <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4.9/5.3/4.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4.9</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>5.3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4.9/5.3/4.9</annotation></semantics></math>. Mask mAP follows the same trend at <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="43.9/45.3/46.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>43.9</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>45.3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>46.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">43.9/45.3/46.0</annotation></semantics></math>, exceeding VMamba-T/S/B by <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.2/1.6/1.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>1.6</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>1.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.2/1.6/1.9</annotation></semantics></math>. Under the longer <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="3{\times}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3{\times}</annotation></semantics></math>+MS schedule, GraphScan-Mamba-T/S/B reach <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="51.0/52.0/52.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>51.0</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>52.0</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>52.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">51.0/52.0/52.5</annotation></semantics></math> box mAP and <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="45.3/45.9/46.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>45.3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>45.9</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>46.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">45.3/45.9/46.2</annotation></semantics></math> mask mAP, again leading the strongest Vision SSM at each scale. The gains transfer to dense prediction without modifying the backbone, indicating that the local semantic routing learned during classification yields tokens that remain useful when the network is evaluated against detection-scale spatial structure.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3 </span>Semantic Segmentation on ADE20K</h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Setup.</span>
We adopt UperNet <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">69</a>]</cite> on ADE20K <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib67" title="" class="ltx_ref">76</a>]</cite>, fine-tuning ImageNet-pretrained backbones for 160K iterations at <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="512{\times}512" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>512</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>512</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">512{\times}512</annotation></semantics></math> crops with AdamW and batch size 16. All experiments are implemented in MMSegmentation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib77" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite>. We report single-scale (SS) and multi-scale (MS) mIoU; FLOPs are reported at <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="512{\times}2048" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>512</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2048</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">512{\times}2048</annotation></semantics></math> input.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Results.</span>
Table <a href="#S4.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 4.3 Semantic Segmentation on ADE20K ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Can Graphs Help Vision SSMs See Better?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> summarizes ADE20K accuracy. GraphScan-Mamba-T/S/B reach mIoU (SS) of <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50.9/52.1/53.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>50.9</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>52.1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>53.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50.9/52.1/53.2</annotation></semantics></math>, surpassing VMamba-T/S/B by <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.9/1.5/2.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.9</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>1.5</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.9/1.5/2.2</annotation></semantics></math> and the strongest Vision SSM baseline at each scale by <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="+0.6/+0.9/+1.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.6</mn><mo rspace="0em">/</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mn>0.9</mn><mo rspace="0em">/</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mn>1.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+0.6/+0.9/+1.3</annotation></semantics></math>. Multi-scale tests show analogous improvements (<math id="S4.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="51.8/52.9/53.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>51.8</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>52.9</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>53.6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">51.8/52.9/53.6</annotation></semantics></math>). As discussed in Sec. <a href="#S3.SS4" title="3.4 GraphScan as Selective-Scan Preconditioning ‣ 3 Method ‣ Can Graphs Help Vision SSMs See Better?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>, the local-global structure induced by GraphScan supplies semantically nearby content into the selective scan, which is especially valuable for scene-level segmentation, where two-dimensional adjacency frequently disagrees with raster order.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T4" class="ltx_table">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure ltx_flex_table">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
