<a href="#S4.SS1.p3.1.1.10.1" title="4.1 Image Classification on ImageNet-1K ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Can Graphs Help Vision SSMs See Better?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">§4.1</span></a>.
</span></li>
</ul>
</section>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Analysis of GraphScan-Induced Selective Scan</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix provides a more detailed analysis of how GraphScan modifies the selective scan computation.
The goal is not to prove a task-level generalization guarantee, but to make precise the architectural effect of routing tokens before the SSM.
GraphScan changes both the values entering the recurrent state and the token-dependent selective parameters that control propagation and readout.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Throughout this appendix, we omit batch dimensions and use the notation from Sec. <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Vision Selective Scan Preliminaries ‣ 3 Method ‣ Can Graphs Help Vision SSMs See Better?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>.
All decompositions below are exact unless explicitly stated otherwise.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Selective Scan as a Token-Conditioned Dynamical System</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a visual token sequence <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}=[\mathbf{x}_{1},\ldots,\mathbf{x}_{L}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}=[\mathbf{x}_{1},\ldots,\mathbf{x}_{L}]</annotation></semantics></math>, the Mamba-style selective scan can be written as a token-conditioned dynamical system:</p>
<table id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{H}_{t}=\bar{\mathbf{A}}_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t})\odot\mathbf{H}_{t-1}+\bar{\mathbf{B}}_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t})\odot\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\uparrow_{s}},\qquad\mathbf{y}_{t}=\left\langle\mathbf{H}_{t},\mathbf{c}_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t})^{\uparrow_{D}}\right\rangle_{N_{s}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐜</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}_{t}=\bar{\mathbf{A}}_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t})\odot\mathbf{H}_{t-1}+\bar{\mathbf{B}}_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t})\odot\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\uparrow_{s}},\qquad\mathbf{y}_{t}=\left\langle\mathbf{H}_{t},\mathbf{c}_{t}(\mathbf{x}_{t})^{\uparrow_{D}}\right\rangle_{N_{s}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mathbf{A}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mathbf{A}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mathbf{B}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mathbf{B}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> are post-discretization tensors, while <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐜</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the input-dependent readout.
The dependence on <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> includes the generation of the final positive step size <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\Delta}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝚫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\Delta}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the selective input vector, and the readout vector.
Thus, unlike a linear time-invariant SSM, the recurrence coefficients are functions of the token sequence <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For a zero initial state, the hidden state unrolls as</p>
<table id="A1.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{H}_{t}=\sum_{i=1}^{t}\mathbf{G}_{t,i}\odot\bar{\mathbf{B}}_{i}(\mathbf{x}_{i})\odot\mathbf{x}_{i}^{\uparrow_{s}},\qquad\mathbf{G}_{t,i}=\bigodot_{j=i+1}^{t}\bar{\mathbf{A}}_{j}(\mathbf{x}_{j})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msub><mi>𝐆</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>𝐆</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⨀</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}_{t}=\sum_{i=1}^{t}\mathbf{G}_{t,i}\odot\bar{\mathbf{B}}_{i}(\mathbf{x}_{i})\odot\mathbf{x}_{i}^{\uparrow_{s}},\qquad\mathbf{G}_{t,i}=\bigodot_{j=i+1}^{t}\bar{\mathbf{A}}_{j}(\mathbf{x}_{j}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">This expression makes the sequence geometry explicit: information from token <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> reaches token <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> through the product of the intermediate state transitions along the scan path.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Exact Routed-vs-Base Decomposition</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">GraphScan replaces each token <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> with a routed token <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}^{\prime}_{t}=\mathbf{x}_{t}+\mathbf{m}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}^{\prime}_{t}=\mathbf{x}_{t}+\mathbf{m}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, where, with <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=W_{v}W_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=W_{v}W_{o}</annotation></semantics></math> as in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E4" title="In 3.4 GraphScan as Selective-Scan Preconditioning ‣ 3 Method ‣ Can Graphs Help Vision SSMs See Better?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>),</p>
<table id="A1.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{m}_{t}=\sum_{j\in\mathcal{S}_{r}(t)}\alpha_{tj}\mathbf{x}_{j}M." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{m}_{t}=\sum_{j\in\mathcal{S}_{r}(t)}\alpha_{tj}\mathbf{x}_{j}M.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The routed selective parameters are</p>
<table id="A1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mathbf{A}}^{\prime}_{t}=\bar{\mathbf{A}}_{t}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime}_{t}),\qquad\bar{\mathbf{B}}^{\prime}_{t}=\bar{\mathbf{B}}_{t}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime}_{t}),\qquad\mathbf{c}^{\prime}_{t}=\mathbf{c}_{t}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime}_{t})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐜</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐜</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mathbf{A}}^{\prime}_{t}=\bar{\mathbf{A}}_{t}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime}_{t}),\qquad\bar{\mathbf{B}}^{\prime}_{t}=\bar{\mathbf{B}}_{t}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime}_{t}),\qquad\mathbf{c}^{\prime}_{t}=\mathbf{c}_{t}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime}_{t}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and the routed recurrence is</p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{H}^{\prime}_{t}=\bar{\mathbf{A}}^{\prime}_{t}\odot\mathbf{H}^{\prime}_{t-1}+\bar{\mathbf{B}}^{\prime}_{t}\odot(\mathbf{x}^{\prime}_{t})^{\uparrow_{s}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}^{\prime}_{t}=\bar{\mathbf{A}}^{\prime}_{t}\odot\mathbf{H}^{\prime}_{t-1}+\bar{\mathbf{B}}^{\prime}_{t}\odot(\mathbf{x}^{\prime}_{t})^{\uparrow_{s}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition A.1 (Exact routed-vs-base decomposition).</span>
Let <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\mathbf{H}_{t}=\mathbf{H}^{\prime}_{t}-\mathbf{H}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\mathbf{H}_{t}=\mathbf{H}^{\prime}_{t}-\mathbf{H}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and define</p>
<table id="A1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\bar{\mathbf{A}}_{t}=\bar{\mathbf{A}}^{\prime}_{t}-\bar{\mathbf{A}}_{t},\qquad\delta\bar{\mathbf{B}}_{t}=\bar{\mathbf{B}}^{\prime}_{t}-\bar{\mathbf{B}}_{t},\qquad\delta\mathbf{c}_{t}=\mathbf{c}^{\prime}_{t}-\mathbf{c}_{t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐜</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐜</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐜</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\bar{\mathbf{A}}_{t}=\bar{\mathbf{A}}^{\prime}_{t}-\bar{\mathbf{A}}_{t},\qquad\delta\bar{\mathbf{B}}_{t}=\bar{\mathbf{B}}^{\prime}_{t}-\bar{\mathbf{B}}_{t},\qquad\delta\mathbf{c}_{t}=\mathbf{c}^{\prime}_{t}-\mathbf{c}_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Assuming the base and routed recurrences share the same initial state, <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\mathbf{H}_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\mathbf{H}_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\delta\mathbf{H}_{t}=\sum_{i=1}^{t}\mathbf{G}^{\prime}_{t,i}\odot\left[\bar{\mathbf{B}}^{\prime}_{i}\odot\mathbf{m}_{i}^{\uparrow_{s}}+\delta\bar{\mathbf{B}}_{i}\odot\mathbf{x}_{i}^{\uparrow_{s}}+\delta\bar{\mathbf{A}}_{i}\odot\mathbf{H}_{i-1}\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>𝐆</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\mathbf{H}_{t}=\sum_{i=1}^{t}\mathbf{G}^{\prime}_{t,i}\odot\left[\bar{\mathbf{B}}^{\prime}_{i}\odot\mathbf{m}_{i}^{\uparrow_{s}}+\delta\bar{\mathbf{B}}_{i}\odot\mathbf{x}_{i}^{\uparrow_{s}}+\delta\bar{\mathbf{A}}_{i}\odot\mathbf{H}_{i-1}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{G}^{\prime}_{t,i}=\bigodot_{j=i+1}^{t}\bar{\mathbf{A}}^{\prime}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐆</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>⨀</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{G}^{\prime}_{t,i}=\bigodot_{j=i+1}^{t}\bar{\mathbf{A}}^{\prime}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{G}^{\prime}_{t,t}=\mathbf{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐆</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{G}^{\prime}_{t,t}=\mathbf{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover,</p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\delta\mathbf{y}_{t}=\left\langle\delta\mathbf{H}_{t},(\mathbf{c}^{\prime}_{t})^{\uparrow_{D}}\right\rangle_{N_{s}}+\left\langle\mathbf{H}_{t},\delta\mathbf{c}_{t}^{\uparrow_{D}}\right\rangle_{N_{s}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐜</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><msubsup><mi>𝐜</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\mathbf{y}_{t}=\left\langle\delta\mathbf{H}_{t},(\mathbf{c}^{\prime}_{t})^{\uparrow_{D}}\right\rangle_{N_{s}}+\left\langle\mathbf{H}_{t},\delta\mathbf{c}_{t}^{\uparrow_{D}}\right\rangle_{N_{s}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof.</span>
Subtract the base recurrence from the routed recurrence.
Using <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}^{\prime}_{t}=\mathbf{x}_{t}+\mathbf{m}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}^{\prime}_{t}=\mathbf{x}_{t}+\mathbf{m}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}^{\prime}_{t-1}=\mathbf{H}_{t-1}+\delta\mathbf{H}_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}^{\prime}_{t-1}=\mathbf{H}_{t-1}+\delta\mathbf{H}_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mathbf{A}}^{\prime}_{t}=\bar{\mathbf{A}}_{t}+\delta\bar{\mathbf{A}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mathbf{A}}^{\prime}_{t}=\bar{\mathbf{A}}_{t}+\delta\bar{\mathbf{A}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mathbf{B}}^{\prime}_{t}=\bar{\mathbf{B}}_{t}+\delta\bar{\mathbf{B}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mathbf{B}}^{\prime}_{t}=\bar{\mathbf{B}}_{t}+\delta\bar{\mathbf{B}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</p>
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex4X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\delta\mathbf{H}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\delta\mathbf{H}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\bar{\mathbf{A}}^{\prime}_{t}\odot(\mathbf{H}_{t-1}+\delta\mathbf{H}_{t-1})+\bar{\mathbf{B}}^{\prime}_{t}\odot(\mathbf{x}_{t}+\mathbf{m}_{t})^{\uparrow_{s}}-\bar{\mathbf{A}}_{t}\odot\mathbf{H}_{t-1}-\bar{\mathbf{B}}_{t}\odot\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\uparrow_{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bar{\mathbf{A}}^{\prime}_{t}\odot(\mathbf{H}_{t-1}+\delta\mathbf{H}_{t-1})+\bar{\mathbf{B}}^{\prime}_{t}\odot(\mathbf{x}_{t}+\mathbf{m}_{t})^{\uparrow_{s}}-\bar{\mathbf{A}}_{t}\odot\mathbf{H}_{t-1}-\bar{\mathbf{B}}_{t}\odot\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\uparrow_{s}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex4Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\bar{\mathbf{A}}^{\prime}_{t}\odot\delta\mathbf{H}_{t-1}+(\bar{\mathbf{A}}^{\prime}_{t}-\bar{\mathbf{A}}_{t})\odot\mathbf{H}_{t-1}+\bar{\mathbf{B}}^{\prime}_{t}\odot\mathbf{m}_{t}^{\uparrow_{s}}+(\bar{\mathbf{B}}^{\prime}_{t}-\bar{\mathbf{B}}_{t})\odot\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\uparrow_{s}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bar{\mathbf{A}}^{\prime}_{t}\odot\delta\mathbf{H}_{t-1}+(\bar{\mathbf{A}}^{\prime}_{t}-\bar{\mathbf{A}}_{t})\odot\mathbf{H}_{t-1}+\bar{\mathbf{B}}^{\prime}_{t}\odot\mathbf{m}_{t}^{\uparrow_{s}}+(\bar{\mathbf{B}}^{\prime}_{t}-\bar{\mathbf{B}}_{t})\odot\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\uparrow_{s}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\delta\mathbf{H}_{t}=\bar{\mathbf{A}}^{\prime}_{t}\odot\delta\mathbf{H}_{t-1}+\delta\bar{\mathbf{A}}_{t}\odot\mathbf{H}_{t-1}+\bar{\mathbf{B}}^{\prime}_{t}\odot\mathbf{m}_{t}^{\uparrow_{s}}+\delta\bar{\mathbf{B}}_{t}\odot\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\uparrow_{s}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\mathbf{H}_{t}=\bar{\mathbf{A}}^{\prime}_{t}\odot\delta\mathbf{H}_{t-1}+\delta\bar{\mathbf{A}}_{t}\odot\mathbf{H}_{t-1}+\bar{\mathbf{B}}^{\prime}_{t}\odot\mathbf{m}_{t}^{\uparrow_{s}}+\delta\bar{\mathbf{B}}_{t}\odot\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\uparrow_{s}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Unrolling this recurrence from <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\mathbf{H}_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\mathbf{H}_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math> gives Eq. (<a href="#A1.E14" title="In A.2 Exact Routed-vs-Base Decomposition ‣ Appendix A Analysis of GraphScan-Induced Selective Scan ‣ Can Graphs Help Vision SSMs See Better?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>).
For the output, write <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}^{\prime}_{t}=\mathbf{H}_{t}+\delta\mathbf{H}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}^{\prime}_{t}=\mathbf{H}_{t}+\delta\mathbf{H}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}^{\prime}_{t}=\mathbf{c}_{t}+\delta\mathbf{c}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐜</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐜</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐜</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}^{\prime}_{t}=\mathbf{c}_{t}+\delta\mathbf{c}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then</p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex6X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\delta\mathbf{y}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\delta\mathbf{y}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\langle\mathbf{H}^{\prime}_{t},(\mathbf{c}^{\prime}_{t})^{\uparrow_{D}}\right\rangle_{N_{s}}-\left\langle\mathbf{H}_{t},\mathbf{c}_{t}^{\uparrow_{D}}\right\rangle_{N_{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo>⟨</mo><mi>𝐇</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>⟩</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><mo>⟨</mo><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>⟩</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\langle\mathbf{H}^{\prime}_{t},(\mathbf{c}^{\prime}_{t})^{\uparrow_{D}}\right\rangle_{N_{s}}-\left\langle\mathbf{H}_{t},\mathbf{c}_{t}^{\uparrow_{D}}\right\rangle_{N_{s}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex6Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\langle\mathbf{H}_{t}+\delta\mathbf{H}_{t},(\mathbf{c}^{\prime}_{t})^{\uparrow_{D}}\right\rangle_{N_{s}}-\left\langle\mathbf{H}_{t},\mathbf{c}_{t}^{\uparrow_{D}}\right\rangle_{N_{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo>⟨</mo><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>⟩</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><mo>⟨</mo><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>⟩</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\langle\mathbf{H}_{t}+\delta\mathbf{H}_{t},(\mathbf{c}^{\prime}_{t})^{\uparrow_{D}}\right\rangle_{N_{s}}-\left\langle\mathbf{H}_{t},\mathbf{c}_{t}^{\uparrow_{D}}\right\rangle_{N_{s}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex6Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\langle\delta\mathbf{H}_{t},(\mathbf{c}^{\prime}_{t})^{\uparrow_{D}}\right\rangle_{N_{s}}+\left\langle\mathbf{H}_{t},(\mathbf{c}^{\prime}_{t}-\mathbf{c}_{t})^{\uparrow_{D}}\right\rangle_{N_{s}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo>⟨</mo><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>⟩</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><mo>⟨</mo><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>⟩</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\langle\delta\mathbf{H}_{t},(\mathbf{c}^{\prime}_{t})^{\uparrow_{D}}\right\rangle_{N_{s}}+\left\langle\mathbf{H}_{t},(\mathbf{c}^{\prime}_{t}-\mathbf{c}_{t})^{\uparrow_{D}}\right\rangle_{N_{s}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p">This proves Eq. (<a href="#A1.E15" title="In A.2 Exact Routed-vs-Base Decomposition ‣ Appendix A Analysis of GraphScan-Induced Selective Scan ‣ Can Graphs Help Vision SSMs See Better?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>).  <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Interpretation.</span>
Eq. (<a href="#A1.E14" title="In A.2 Exact Routed-vs-Base Decomposition ‣ Appendix A Analysis of GraphScan-Induced Selective Scan ‣ Can Graphs Help Vision SSMs See Better?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>) separates three hidden-state pathways: direct routed value injection, write modulation, and transition modulation.
Eq. (<a href="#A1.E15" title="In A.2 Exact Routed-vs-Base Decomposition ‣ Appendix A Analysis of GraphScan-Induced Selective Scan ‣ Can Graphs Help Vision SSMs See Better?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>) adds a fourth pathway: readout modulation.
The decomposition is exact and does not rely on treating the GraphScan message as small.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Local-Global Kernel Induced by GraphScan</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now isolate the direct routed value path in Eq. (<a href="#A1.E14" title="In A.2 Exact Routed-vs-Base Decomposition ‣ Appendix A Analysis of GraphScan-Induced Selective Scan ‣ Can Graphs Help Vision SSMs See Better?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>).
Define the routed SSM input-to-output operator</p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{K}^{\prime}_{t,i}(\mathbf{z})=\left\langle\mathbf{G}^{\prime}_{t,i}\odot\bar{\mathbf{B}}^{\prime}_{i}\odot\mathbf{z}^{\uparrow_{s}},(\mathbf{c}^{\prime}_{t})^{\uparrow_{D}}\right\rangle_{N_{s}},\qquad i\leq t." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐆</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐜</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}^{\prime}_{t,i}(\mathbf{z})=\left\langle\mathbf{G}^{\prime}_{t,i}\odot\bar{\mathbf{B}}^{\prime}_{i}\odot\mathbf{z}^{\uparrow_{s}},(\mathbf{c}^{\prime}_{t})^{\uparrow_{D}}\right\rangle_{N_{s}},\qquad i\leq t.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&gt;t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&gt;t</annotation></semantics></math>, set <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}^{\prime}_{t,i}(\mathbf{z})=\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}^{\prime}_{t,i}(\mathbf{z})=\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary A.2 (Local-global kernel composition).</span>
The direct routed value contribution to <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\mathbf{y}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\mathbf{y}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\delta\mathbf{y}^{\mathrm{route}}_{t}=\sum_{j=1}^{L}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}i\leq t:\\
j\in\mathcal{S}_{r}(i)\end{subarray}}\alpha_{ij}\,\mathcal{K}^{\prime}_{t,i}(\mathbf{x}_{j}M)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>route</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\mathbf{y}^{\mathrm{route}}_{t}=\sum_{j=1}^{L}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}i\leq t:\\
j\in\mathcal{S}_{r}(i)\end{subarray}}\alpha_{ij}\,\mathcal{K}^{\prime}_{t,i}(\mathbf{x}_{j}M).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof.</span>
The direct routed value pathway in Eq. (<a href="#A1.E14" title="In A.2 Exact Routed-vs-Base Decomposition ‣ Appendix A Analysis of GraphScan-Induced Selective Scan ‣ Can Graphs Help Vision SSMs See Better?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>) contributes</p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\delta\mathbf{y}^{\mathrm{route}}_{t}=\left\langle\sum_{i=1}^{t}\mathbf{G}^{\prime}_{t,i}\odot\bar{\mathbf{B}}^{\prime}_{i}\odot\mathbf{m}_{i}^{\uparrow_{s}},(\mathbf{c}^{\prime}_{t})^{\uparrow_{D}}\right\rangle_{N_{s}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>route</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>𝐆</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐜</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\mathbf{y}^{\mathrm{route}}_{t}=\left\langle\sum_{i=1}^{t}\mathbf{G}^{\prime}_{t,i}\odot\bar{\mathbf{B}}^{\prime}_{i}\odot\mathbf{m}_{i}^{\uparrow_{s}},(\mathbf{c}^{\prime}_{t})^{\uparrow_{D}}\right\rangle_{N_{s}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">By the definition of <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}^{\prime}_{t,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}^{\prime}_{t,i}</annotation></semantics></math>, this equals</p>
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\mathbf{y}^{\mathrm{route}}_{t}=\sum_{i=1}^{t}\mathcal{K}^{\prime}_{t,i}(\mathbf{m}_{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>route</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\mathbf{y}^{\mathrm{route}}_{t}=\sum_{i=1}^{t}\mathcal{K}^{\prime}_{t,i}(\mathbf{m}_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Substituting <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{m}_{i}=\sum_{j\in\mathcal{S}_{r}(i)}\alpha_{ij}\mathbf{x}_{j}M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{m}_{i}=\sum_{j\in\mathcal{S}_{r}(i)}\alpha_{ij}\mathbf{x}_{j}M</annotation></semantics></math> gives</p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\mathbf{y}^{\mathrm{route}}_{t}=\sum_{i=1}^{t}\mathcal{K}^{\prime}_{t,i}\left(\sum_{j\in\mathcal{S}_{r}(i)}\alpha_{ij}\mathbf{x}_{j}M\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>route</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\mathbf{y}^{\mathrm{route}}_{t}=\sum_{i=1}^{t}\mathcal{K}^{\prime}_{t,i}\left(\sum_{j\in\mathcal{S}_{r}(i)}\alpha_{ij}\mathbf{x}_{j}M\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.4" class="ltx_p">For fixed routed coefficients, <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}^{\prime}_{t,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}^{\prime}_{t,i}</annotation></semantics></math> is linear in its argument.
Therefore,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\mathbf{y}^{\mathrm{route}}_{t}=\sum_{i=1}^{t}\sum_{j\in\mathcal{S}_{r}(i)}\alpha_{ij}\,\mathcal{K}^{\prime}_{t,i}(\mathbf{x}_{j}M)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>route</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\mathbf{y}^{\mathrm{route}}_{t}=\sum_{i=1}^{t}\sum_{j\in\mathcal{S}_{r}(i)}\alpha_{ij}\,\mathcal{K}^{\prime}_{t,i}(\mathbf{x}_{j}M).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.5" class="ltx_p">Exchanging the finite sums over <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> gives Eq. (<a href="#A1.E17" title="In A.3 Local-Global Kernel Induced by GraphScan ‣ Appendix A Analysis of GraphScan-Induced Selective Scan ‣ Can Graphs Help Vision SSMs See Better?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>).  <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Interpretation.</span>
Eq. (<a href="#A1.E17" title="In A.3 Local-Global Kernel Induced by GraphScan ‣ Appendix A Analysis of GraphScan-Induced Selective Scan ‣ Can Graphs Help Vision SSMs See Better?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>) shows that GraphScan composes two kernels.
The first is a local semantic kernel <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> defined over a bounded two-dimensional neighborhood.
The second is a global selective SSM kernel <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}^{\prime}_{t,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}^{\prime}_{t,i}</annotation></semantics></math> defined along the one-dimensional scan path.
Thus, GraphScan does not replace the SSM with local attention; it composes local semantic routing with global state-space propagation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Scan-Distance Shortcuts under Bounded Survival</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The local-global kernel clarifies why routing can help when two-dimensional adjacency is poorly aligned with raster order.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition A.3 (Semantic shortcut under bounded routed survival).</span>
Assume the routed selective transitions satisfy <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bar{\mathbf{A}}^{\prime}_{j}\|_{\infty}\leq\rho&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bar{\mathbf{A}}^{\prime}_{j}\|_{\infty}\leq\rho&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, and assume <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bar{\mathbf{B}}^{\prime}_{i}\|_{\infty}\leq B_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bar{\mathbf{B}}^{\prime}_{i}\|_{\infty}\leq B_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{c}^{\prime}_{t}\|_{\infty}\leq C_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐜</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{c}^{\prime}_{t}\|_{\infty}\leq C_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, for any <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\leq t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\leq t</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathcal{K}^{\prime}_{t,i}(\mathbf{z})\|_{\infty}\leq N_{s}B_{\max}C_{\max}\rho^{t-i}\|\mathbf{z}\|_{\infty}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathcal{K}^{\prime}_{t,i}(\mathbf{z})\|_{\infty}\leq N_{s}B_{\max}C_{\max}\rho^{t-i}\|\mathbf{z}\|_{\infty}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Consequently, a source token routed through slot <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> contributes to output <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> with attenuation governed by the scan distance <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t-i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t-i</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof.</span>
By definition,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{G}^{\prime}_{t,i}=\bigodot_{\ell=i+1}^{t}\bar{\mathbf{A}}^{\prime}_{\ell}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐆</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⨀</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{G}^{\prime}_{t,i}=\bigodot_{\ell=i+1}^{t}\bar{\mathbf{A}}^{\prime}_{\ell}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Using submultiplicativity of the elementwise <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> norm under Hadamard products and the assumption <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bar{\mathbf{A}}^{\prime}_{\ell}\|_{\infty}\leq\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bar{\mathbf{A}}^{\prime}_{\ell}\|_{\infty}\leq\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</p>
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{G}^{\prime}_{t,i}\|_{\infty}\leq\prod_{\ell=i+1}^{t}\|\bar{\mathbf{A}}^{\prime}_{\ell}\|_{\infty}\leq\rho^{t-i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐆</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{G}^{\prime}_{t,i}\|_{\infty}\leq\prod_{\ell=i+1}^{t}\|\bar{\mathbf{A}}^{\prime}_{\ell}\|_{\infty}\leq\rho^{t-i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.3" class="ltx_p">For each output channel <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-th component of <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}^{\prime}_{t,i}(\mathbf{z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}^{\prime}_{t,i}(\mathbf{z})</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\mathcal{K}^{\prime}_{t,i}(\mathbf{z})]_{d}=\sum_{n=1}^{N_{s}}[\mathbf{G}^{\prime}_{t,i}]_{d,n}[\bar{\mathbf{B}}^{\prime}_{i}]_{d,n}z_{d}[\mathbf{c}^{\prime}_{t}]_{n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐆</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐜</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\mathcal{K}^{\prime}_{t,i}(\mathbf{z})]_{d}=\sum_{n=1}^{N_{s}}[\mathbf{G}^{\prime}_{t,i}]_{d,n}[\bar{\mathbf{B}}^{\prime}_{i}]_{d,n}z_{d}[\mathbf{c}^{\prime}_{t}]_{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Taking absolute values and applying the bounds on <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{G}^{\prime}_{t,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐆</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{G}^{\prime}_{t,i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mathbf{B}}^{\prime}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mathbf{B}}^{\prime}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}^{\prime}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐜</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}^{\prime}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|[\mathcal{K}^{\prime}_{t,i}(\mathbf{z})]_{d}|\leq\sum_{n=1}^{N_{s}}\rho^{t-i}B_{\max}C_{\max}\|\mathbf{z}\|_{\infty}=N_{s}B_{\max}C_{\max}\rho^{t-i}\|\mathbf{z}\|_{\infty}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|[\mathcal{K}^{\prime}_{t,i}(\mathbf{z})]_{d}|\leq\sum_{n=1}^{N_{s}}\rho^{t-i}B_{\max}C_{\max}\|\mathbf{z}\|_{\infty}=N_{s}B_{\max}C_{\max}\rho^{t-i}\|\mathbf{z}\|_{\infty}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.5" class="ltx_p">Taking the maximum over channels <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> proves Eq. (<a href="#A1.E18" title="In A.4 Scan-Distance Shortcuts under Bounded Survival ‣ Appendix A Analysis of GraphScan-Induced Selective Scan ‣ Can Graphs Help Vision SSMs See Better?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>).  <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Interpretation.</span>
This result does not claim GraphScan always improves accuracy.
It shows a structural effect: a source patch can influence the SSM through a routed slot whose scan distance to the output may differ from the source patch’s raster distance.
When two-dimensional adjacency and one-dimensional raster order disagree, GraphScan supplies additional local semantic paths into the selective scan.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Reachability View from State-Space Systems</h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If the selective coefficients are frozen, Eq. (<a href="#A1.E10" title="In A.1 Selective Scan as a Token-Conditioned Dynamical System ‣ Appendix A Analysis of GraphScan-Induced Selective Scan ‣ Can Graphs Help Vision SSMs See Better?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>) becomes a linear time-varying state-space system.
Classical control theory studies how inputs enter such systems through transition operators and input matrices, often through reachability or controllability analyses <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib71" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>, <a href="#bib.bib72" title="" class="ltx_ref">49</a>]</cite>.
GraphScan modifies the input directions before they are injected into the recurrent state.
In the frozen-coefficient view, the base system is driven by isolated raster tokens, while the routed system is driven by locally aggregated semantic neighborhoods.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">More explicitly, with frozen coefficients and zero initial state, the base hidden state is</p>
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{H}_{t}=\sum_{i=1}^{t}\mathbf{G}_{t,i}\odot\bar{\mathbf{B}}_{i}\odot\mathbf{x}_{i}^{\uparrow_{s}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐇</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mi>𝐆</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}_{t}=\sum_{i=1}^{t}\mathbf{G}_{t,i}\odot\bar{\mathbf{B}}_{i}\odot\mathbf{x}_{i}^{\uparrow_{s}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">With GraphScan-routed inputs but the same frozen coefficients, the hidden state becomes</p>
<table id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{H}^{\mathrm{gs}}_{t}=\sum_{i=1}^{t}\mathbf{G}_{t,i}\odot\bar{\mathbf{B}}_{i}\odot\left(\mathbf{x}_{i}+\sum_{j\in\mathcal{S}_{r}(i)}\alpha_{ij}\mathbf{x}_{j}M\right)^{\uparrow_{s}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>gs</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msub><mi>𝐆</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>M</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}^{\mathrm{gs}}_{t}=\sum_{i=1}^{t}\mathbf{G}_{t,i}\odot\bar{\mathbf{B}}_{i}\odot\left(\mathbf{x}_{i}+\sum_{j\in\mathcal{S}_{r}(i)}\alpha_{ij}\mathbf{x}_{j}M\right)^{\uparrow_{s}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Eq. (<a href="#A1.E20" title="In A.5 Reachability View from State-Space Systems ‣ Appendix A Analysis of GraphScan-Induced Selective Scan ‣ Can Graphs Help Vision SSMs See Better?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>) shows that GraphScan changes the finite-horizon input-to-state map by introducing cross-token input directions induced by the sparse routing matrix <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(\mathbf{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(\mathbf{X})</annotation></semantics></math>.
The recurrent state is no longer driven only by isolated raster tokens; it is also driven by local semantic combinations of nearby tokens.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This reachability view should be interpreted carefully: GraphScan does not guarantee better controllability or generalization in the formal control-theoretic sense without additional assumptions.
Instead, it provides a structural mechanism by which the finite recurrent state receives richer local semantic inputs before global propagation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.6 </span>Baseline Containment</h3>

<div id="A1.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition A.4 (Baseline containment).</span>
GraphScan-Mamba contains the corresponding base Vision Mamba model as a subnetwork.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof.</span>
From Eq. (<a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.3 GraphScan: Local Semantic Routing ‣ 3 Method ‣ Can Graphs Help Vision SSMs See Better?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), setting <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{o}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{o}=0</annotation></semantics></math> makes the routed message vanish for every token, so <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}^{\prime}_{i}=\mathbf{x}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}^{\prime}_{i}=\mathbf{x}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
If an implementation includes a bias in the output projection, setting that bias to zero as well gives the same identity map.
Equivalently, Eq. (<a href="#S3.E4" title="In 3.4 GraphScan as Selective-Scan Preconditioning ‣ 3 Method ‣ Can Graphs Help Vision SSMs See Better?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) reduces to <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}^{\prime}=\mathbf{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}^{\prime}=\mathbf{X}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The subsequent selective SSM, residual branches, feed-forward layers, and classifier are then identical to those of the corresponding base Vision Mamba model.
Therefore, the base model is obtained as a parameter setting of GraphScan-Mamba.  <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS6.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Interpretation.</span>
This containment result does not imply optimization will always find a better solution, but it shows that GraphScan preserves the base model as a special case while adding trainable local routing paths before the SSM.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.7 </span>Relation to Local Attention and Vision GNNs</h3>

<div id="A1.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">GraphScan uses a primitive related to local neighborhood attention and graph message passing.
Neighborhood attention restricts Q/K/V attention to a sliding neighborhood around each token, providing an efficient local attention mechanism for hierarchical Transformer backbones <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>; non-local networks generalize visual feature aggregation through pairwise interactions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib75" title="" class="ltx_ref">64</a>]</cite>.
Vision GNNs instead view image patches as graph nodes and perform learned neighborhood aggregation over visual tokens <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>, <a href="#bib.bib69" title="" class="ltx_ref">66</a>]</cite>, building on the broader graph-network and message-passing primitives studied in deep learning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib73" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>, <a href="#bib.bib74" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>.
GraphScan borrows this local affinity aggregation primitive, but uses it in a different role: it is not the main token mixer of a Transformer or GNN backbone.
It is a scan-time preconditioner placed immediately before the selective SSM.
As shown above, this placement causes local semantic routing to influence both the values entering the recurrent state and the token-conditioned parameters of the selective scan.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Extended Related Work</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix expands the condensed related work in Sec. <a href="#S2" title="2 Related Work ‣ Can Graphs Help Vision SSMs See Better?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> with the fuller treatment across all four prior-work paradigms.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Vision Backbones</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Visual backbone design has evolved through several representation paradigms.
Convolutional neural networks model images as regular grids and encode locality through sliding filters, hierarchical downsampling, residual connections, scaling rules, and large-kernel convolutional blocks <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>, <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>, <a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">47</a>, <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>, <a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>, <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>, <a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">51</a>, <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">43</a>, <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>, <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">65</a>, <a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>, <a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>, <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">74</a>]</cite>.
Vision Transformers recast images as sequences of patch tokens and use self-attention for flexible long-range interaction <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">57</a>, <a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>, <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">55</a>]</cite>.
To support high-resolution recognition and dense prediction, later Transformer backbones introduced hierarchical designs, shifted or windowed attention, pyramid structures, cross-shaped and focal attention, neighborhood attention, deformable attention, bi-level routing, non-local interactions, and convolution-attention hybrids <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>, <a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">62</a>, <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">63</a>, <a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>, <a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>, <a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">73</a>, <a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>, <a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">67</a>, <a href="#bib.bib75" title="" class="ltx_ref">64</a>, <a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">77</a>, <a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">56</a>, <a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>, <a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, <a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">61</a>]</cite>.
Beyond convolution and attention, all-MLP models explore token mixing with feed-forward layers <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">53</a>, <a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">54</a>, <a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite>, while Vision GNNs view image patches as graph nodes and propagate information through learned neighborhood aggregation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>, <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">58</a>, <a href="#bib.bib73" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>, <a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>, <a href="#bib.bib69" title="" class="ltx_ref">66</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">GraphScan is related to this graph-based view, but it is not a standalone Vision GNN backbone.
Instead, it uses lightweight local graph routing inside a Vision SSM, enriching visual tokens with semantic neighborhood context before global state-space mixing.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>State Space Sequence Models</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Structured state space models provide efficient sequence modeling with long-range interactions and linear or near-linear scaling in sequence length <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>, <a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>, <a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">48</a>]</cite>.
Early SSM-based architectures such as H3 and Hyena demonstrated the promise of long convolutional and state-space sequence mixers as alternatives to attention <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>, <a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>]</cite>.
Mamba introduced selective state spaces, making key SSM parameters input-dependent so that the model can selectively propagate, reset, or ignore information along the sequence while retaining efficient scan-based computation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite>.
Mamba-2 further connected SSMs and attention through structured state space duality and improved the efficiency of the core sequence mixer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>.
Mamba-3 extends this line with recurrence-level improvements such as exponential-trapezoidal discretization, complex-valued state transitions, and MIMO updates <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">These works improve the sequence model itself.
Our work addresses a complementary question that arises when such models are used for vision: how should a two-dimensional visual feature map be routed before it is processed by a one-dimensional state-space operator?</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Vision Mamba and Scan Design</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Vision Mamba models adapt selective SSMs to images by converting feature maps into token sequences.
Vim applies bidirectional Mamba blocks to visual sequences, while VMamba introduces a two-dimensional selective scan to process visual features along multiple spatial directions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">78</a>, <a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite>.
Since scan order determines how two-dimensional structure is exposed to the one-dimensional recurrence, subsequent work has explored increasingly structured scan patterns.
Continuous scans improve spatial continuity <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">72</a>]</cite>; local-window scans preserve short-range dependencies and search layer-wise scan choices <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>]</cite>; atrous and multi-scale scans improve efficiency and hierarchical coverage <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>, <a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">45</a>]</cite>; grouped and multidimensional scans distribute scanning across channels or spatial axes <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>, <a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>]</cite>; and fractal or space-filling scans aim to preserve locality under serialization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">These methods show that scan design is central to Vision SSM performance.
However, most of them rely on predefined traversal patterns or layer-level choices, rather than input-dependent semantic routing.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Dynamic and Relational Scanning</h3>

<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recent work investigates adaptive scanning for Vision SSMs.
Quadtree-based scan methods learn spatial partitions with varying granularity <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">71</a>]</cite>.
Coordinate-offset methods predict deformable sampling locations and construct routed tokens through bilinear interpolation before feeding them to the SSM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>, <a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>]</cite>.
Other approaches reorder or prioritize tokens using task- or content-dependent scores, or use similarity signals in specialized correspondence settings <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">75</a>, <a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">60</a>, <a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite>.
PVMamba modifies hidden-state generation through dynamic state aggregation and spatial sampling to reduce sequential constraints <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">70</a>]</cite>.
Spatial-Mamba introduces structure-aware fusion in the state space <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">68</a>]</cite>, VSSD reformulates SSD into a non-causal visual operator <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite>, and MambaVision hybridizes Mamba and Transformer blocks for high-level visual modeling <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">GraphScan occupies a distinct design space.
Rather than changing the SSM recurrence, collapsing scan order, or predicting continuous coordinates, GraphScan learns a local semantic graph over visual tokens and performs one-step message passing before the SSM.
It is input-adaptive like dynamic scans, spatially bounded like local scans, and semantic like graph message passing.
Consequently, the global selective SSM receives tokens that are already locally grounded, while preserving token count and linear scaling.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
