<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Visualizations</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Capturing the per-block attention weights of the trained GraphScan-Mamba-S backbone surfaces two patterns. (i) <em id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Stage-3 outer-ring specialization</em> (Fig. <a href="#A4.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Appendix D Visualizations ‣ Can Graphs Help Vision SSMs See Better?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>): the depthwise <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3{\times}3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3{\times}3</annotation></semantics></math> convolution that runs before GraphScan already aggregates the inner <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3{\times}3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3{\times}3</annotation></semantics></math> block into the query, so the operator suppresses the inner ring by roughly <math id="A4.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="40\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>40</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">40\times</annotation></semantics></math> below uniform and attends almost exclusively to the <math id="A4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\infty}{=}2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\infty}{=}2</annotation></semantics></math> outer ring—specializing in cells the preceding convolution cannot reach. (ii) <em id="A4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Stage-4 convergent global routing</em> (Fig. <a href="#A4.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Appendix D Visualizations ‣ Can Graphs Help Vision SSMs See Better?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>): with the local window covering the full <math id="A4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7{\times}7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7{\times}7</annotation></semantics></math> feature map, the displacement field <math id="A4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\widehat{\mathbf{p}}_{i}=\sum_{j}\alpha_{ij}(\mathbf{p}_{j}-\mathbf{p}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\widehat{\mathbf{p}}_{i}=\sum_{j}\alpha_{ij}(\mathbf{p}_{j}-\mathbf{p}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> converges onto salient object content and the effective scan path collapses there rather than tracing the spatial grid.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F4" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2605.11300v1/stage3_attention.png" id="A4.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/171;" width="476" height="171" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span><span id="A4.F4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stage-3 GraphScan attention</span> on two ImageNet val images. For each query patch (yellow box), the <math id="A4.F4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="14{\times}14" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>14</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">14{\times}14</annotation></semantics></math> attention heatmap concentrates on the <math id="A4.F4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\infty}{=}2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\infty}{=}2</annotation></semantics></math> outer ring; the central <math id="A4.F4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3{\times}3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3{\times}3</annotation></semantics></math> block is suppressed because the preceding depthwise convolution already covers it.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2605.11300v1/stage4_routing.png" id="A4.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/127;" width="476" height="127" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span><span id="A4.F5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stage-4 effective routing.</span> Per-patch displacement field (HSV by direction) and the polyline visiting displaced positions in raster order (plasma, start <math id="A4.F5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bullet" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#008000;" mathcolor="#008000">∙</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bullet</annotation></semantics></math>, end <math id="A4.F5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\blacksquare" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" mathvariant="normal">■</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\blacksquare</annotation></semantics></math>). Both converge onto the discriminative object content.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
